cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the released version-specific software DOI and dataset. This working tree adds the extended experiment pending a new release."
title: "GEOMAPS: sparse-pyramid MVT and MLT compression"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23456861"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/goodlancer-org/mvt-mlt-granularity"
abstract: >-
  Code for "Does Tile Granularity Matter? An Empirical Study of Vector Tile
  Compression for Map Rendering with MapLibre Tiles": vector-source
  normalization, exact Standard/Aggregated-4/Aggregated-16 controls, regenerated
  Dense-4/Dense-16 tiles, pinned Rust MLT v1/v2 encoding, feature provenance,
  matched-block effect decomposition, validation, and automatic figures,
  manuscript tables and SQLite/Parquet/CSV exports. Historical results remain separate.
keywords:
  - vector tiles
  - MapLibre
  - MLT
  - MVT
  - PMTiles
  - compression
  - tile granularity
